{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# The third live-DC channel never got bug 9790's readiness rule\n\nFound by the parity sweep while fixing [rebar:9790-cafa-dffa-462e].\n\n`.github/workflows/jira-dc-capability-map.yml:83` gates on the same cheap\n`curl .../rest/api/2/serverInfo` loop the other two live-DC workflows use, then at line 111 runs\n`python scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py` — whose explicit job (`scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py:401-402`)\nis to record \"the ids of `Epic Link` and `Epic Name`\" as the DECLARED environment contract.\n\nThat script performs **no wait for the fields to register**. 9790 measured, on probe run\n30944211742, that `serverInfo` goes green at 8m32s and the field inventory one second later is 27\nfields, every one a system field, no `customfield_*`.\n\n## Why this is worse than the case 9790 fixed\n\nThe harness and the probe fail LOUDLY when the fields are missing. The capability map does not\nfail — it **reports**, and its report is the authority a human uses to update `_REQUIRED_FIELDS` /\n`_PROJECT_TEMPLATE` in `tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py`. A run landing inside the\nregistration window would record \"Epic Link absent from this image\" as the declared contract. The\nmitigations are real but partial: the job is `workflow_dispatch`-only, the agent emits the raw\nrequest/response evidence, and a human reviews before anything is committed — so a reader who\nnotices \"zero customfield_* entries\" can catch it. Nothing makes them notice.\n\n## Fix\n\nCall the shared definition landed by 9790 — `scripts/jira_dc_field_readiness.await_required_fields`\n— at the top of `main()`, before the agent run begins, and abort with `not_ready_message(...)` when\nthe budget expires. The module is stdlib-only and sits in the same directory, so it is a plain\nimport.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py` waits for `jira_dc_field_readiness.REQUIRED_FIELDS` to be\n      present in `/rest/api/2/field` before the agent run begins\n- [ ] on expiry it aborts with the shared `not_ready_message` (both candidate causes plus the\n      observed inventory) instead of mapping an inventory it cannot vouch for\n- [ ] a test drives that surface with a system-only inventory and pins that the run aborts rather\n      than reporting the Epic fields as absent from the image\n\n## Testing\n\n    pytest tests/unit/test_jira_dc_capability_map_workflow.py -q\n    make lint && make typecheck"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785898628303493001,"uuid":"cdcc0754-9b6c-406a-a35a-654402172750"}